    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d477-a2">

                <pb facs="0795" n="661" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg661"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 690.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Coleman to Mr. Black.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-11-09"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 9,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    communication of the 7th instant, inclosing the application of Mr. Solomon H.
                    Ulmer for a passport for himself, wife, and minor son, and to inform you that it
                    is deemed best, in view of all the circumstances of the case, to refer the same
                    to the Department of State for its consideration and decision.</p>
                <p>Please inform Mr. Ulmer that this will be done, and return to him at the same
                    time his certificate of naturalization, herewith returned.</p>
                <p>The decision reached in this case will be duly made known to you when
                    communicated to this legation.</p>
                <p>By direction of the minister.</p>
                <p>I remain, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">C. Coleman</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of Legation.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
